\ Deadline: the theme, cool jazz on the synthesizer. A quartet in a smoky
\ room at 72 beats a minute: a tenor saxophone carrying a minor melody, an
\ upright bass playing in two, a piano comping sparse rootless voicings and
\ answering in the gaps, and a three-piece kit played with brushes (a snare
\ swept and tapped, a hi-hat closed by the foot on two and four, a bass drum
\ feathered on one and three). Twenty-two bars in D minor: a four-bar piano
\ introduction, the melody twice, and a two-bar ending on D minor with a
\ major seventh. queue-theme queues the whole piece on the sequencer, so it
\ plays live after audio-on or offline through render-audio.

\ === the instruments ===

\ tenor saxophone: 0 sine carrier with light self-feedback and a tremolo, 1 modulator at the note swelling after the onset, 2 octave modulator feeding it, 3 pink breath, 4 third-harmonic modulator for the reed's edge
{ :oscillators [
    { :lfo-level 0.25 :attack 0.05 :decay 0.6 :sustain 0.85 :sustain-decay 8 :release 0.18 }
    { :level 1 :attack 0.09 :decay 0.5 :sustain 0.75 :release 0.18 }
    { :ratio 2 :level 0.55 :attack 0.03 :decay 0.3 :sustain 0.35 :release 0.15 }
    { :wave :pink :level 0.06 :attack 0.03 :decay 0.2 :sustain 0.35 :release 0.12 }
    { :ratio 3 :level 0.5 :attack 0.06 :decay 0.4 :sustain 0.5 :release 0.15 } ]
  :modulation [ [ 1 0 2.6 ] [ 2 1 0.7 ] [ 4 0 0.7 ] [ 0 0 0.3 ] ]
  :carriers [ 0 3 ]
  :cutoff 3400 :resonance 0.6 :drive 1.4
  :filter-envelope { :attack 0.07 :decay 0.5 :sustain 0.55 :release 0.2 :amount 1.1 }
  :lfo { :shape :sine :rate 5 :delay 0.3 :fade 0.5 :pitch-depth 0.18 }
  :glide 0.05 :velocity-sensitivity 0.6 :pan 0.05 :level 0.16 } :sax instrument-patch!

\ clarinet in its low register: 0 a square wave, the odd harmonics of a closed tube, 1 a sine for body, 2 pink breath; a low-pass that brightens at the attack, a slight vibrato entering late, and two copies a few cents apart spread across the stereo field, a chorus of its own
{ :oscillators [
    { :wave :pulse :level 0.7 :attack 0.06 :decay 0.4 :sustain 0.9 :sustain-decay 6 :release 0.15 }
    { :level 0.5 :attack 0.05 :decay 0.4 :sustain 0.9 :sustain-decay 6 :release 0.15 }
    { :wave :pink :level 0.04 :attack 0.03 :decay 0.15 :sustain 0.3 :release 0.1 } ]
  :carriers [ 0 1 2 ]
  :cutoff 1300 :resonance 0.2
  :filter-envelope { :attack 0.06 :decay 0.3 :sustain 0.5 :release 0.15 :amount 0.6 }
  :lfo { :shape :sine :rate 4.8 :delay 0.6 :fade 0.8 :pitch-depth 0.09 }
  :unison 2 :unison-detune 7 :unison-spread 0.35
  :velocity-sensitivity 0.6 :pan 0.1 :level 0.06 } :clarinet instrument-patch!

\ a piano patch at a pan: 0-4 the string's first five partials, stretched sharp as a stiff string's are, each higher one decaying faster; 5 a hammer click on the fundamental; 6 pink hammer noise; two strings beating
: piano-patch ( pan -- patch )
	| pan |
	{ :oscillators [
	    { :attack 0.002 :decay 0.5 :sustain 0.45 :sustain-decay 4 :release 0.3 }
	    { :ratio 2.002 :level 0.55 :attack 0.002 :decay 0.35 :sustain 0.35 :sustain-decay 2.5 :release 0.25 }
	    { :ratio 3.007 :level 0.32 :attack 0.002 :decay 0.25 :sustain 0.25 :sustain-decay 1.5 :release 0.2 }
	    { :ratio 4.015 :level 0.2 :attack 0.002 :decay 0.18 :sustain 0.15 :sustain-decay 0.9 :release 0.15 }
	    { :ratio 5.026 :level 0.12 :attack 0.002 :decay 0.12 :sustain 0.1 :sustain-decay 0.5 :release 0.1 }
	    { :level 0.7 :attack 0.001 :decay 0.03 :sustain 0 :release 0.02 }
	    { :wave :pink :level 0.025 :attack 0.001 :decay 0.012 :sustain 0 :release 0.02 } ]
	  :modulation [ [ 5 0 0.8 ] ]
	  :carriers [ 0 1 2 3 4 6 ]
	  :cutoff 3500 :filter-envelope { :attack 0.001 :decay 0.4 :sustain 0.2 :release 0.3 :amount 1 }
	  :unison 2 :unison-detune 2 :unison-spread 0.3
	  :velocity-sensitivity 0.7 :pan pan :level 0.08 } ;

0.3 piano-patch :piano instrument-patch!
0.4 piano-patch :piano-fill instrument-patch!

\ upright bass, plucked: 0 carrier, 1 modulator at the note for the twang of the pluck, 2 second harmonic, 3 brown thump, 4 white click of the string meeting the fingerboard; no resonance, so the opening filter sweeps without a pitch
{ :oscillators [
    { :attack 0.002 :decay 0.25 :sustain 0.5 :sustain-decay 1.6 :release 0.2 }
    { :level 0.8 :attack 0.001 :decay 0.04 :sustain 0.06 :release 0.2 }
    { :ratio 2 :level 0.25 :attack 0.002 :decay 0.2 :sustain 0.2 :sustain-decay 1.2 :release 0.2 }
    { :wave :brown :level 0.12 :attack 0.001 :decay 0.02 :sustain 0 :release 0.02 }
    { :wave :white :level 0.2 :attack 0.0003 :decay 0.0025 :sustain 0 :release 0.003 } ]
  :modulation [ [ 1 0 1.3 ] ]
  :carriers [ 0 2 3 4 ]
  :cutoff 1100 :filter-envelope { :attack 0.001 :decay 0.02 :sustain 0.1 :release 0.2 :amount 1.6 }
  :velocity-sensitivity 0.5 :pan -0.05 :level 0.36 } :bass instrument-patch!

\ brush swept round the snare head: pink noise swelling and fading, the cutoff circling once a beat
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :pink :attack 0.1 :decay 0.25 :sustain 0.55 :release 0.2 } ]
  :cutoff 2800 :resonance 0.2 :lfo { :shape :sine :rate 1.2 :cutoff-depth 0.6 }
  :velocity-sensitivity 0.8 :pan -0.35 :level 0.07 } :brush instrument-patch!

\ brush pressed on the snare: a burst of pink noise rising over 12 ms, over a faint body
{ :oscillators [
    { :wave :pink :attack 0.012 :decay 0.1 :sustain 0 :release 0.09 }
    { :fixed-hz 185 :level 0.18 :attack 0.01 :decay 0.06 :sustain 0 :release 0.06 } ]
  :carriers [ 0 1 ]
  :cutoff 3800 :pan -0.3 :level 0.2 } :snare instrument-patch!

\ a hi-hat that rings for a time constant: white noise between a high-pass at 6 kHz and the ladder's cutoff
: hihat-patch ( ring cutoff level -- patch )
	| ring cutoff level |
	{ :oscillators [ { :wave :white :attack 0.001 :decay ring :sustain 0 :release ring 0.8 * } ]
	  :high-pass 6000 :cutoff cutoff :pan -0.25 :level level } ;

\ the hi-hat closed by the foot, cut short, and half open, ringing for about a fifth of a second
0.05 11000 0.9 hihat-patch :hihat instrument-patch!
0.22 9000 0.6 hihat-patch :open-hihat instrument-patch!

\ bass drum, feathered: 0 a low sine body, 1 a short thump modulating it, 2 the head's octave decaying faster, 3 the felt beater's click, so the drum carries on small speakers; tuned between B1 and C2 so it never merges with a root the bass plays
{ :oscillators [
    { :fixed-hz 62 :attack 0.002 :decay 0.2 :sustain 0 :release 0.1 }
    { :fixed-hz 100 :attack 0.001 :decay 0.03 :sustain 0 :release 0.03 }
    { :fixed-hz 124 :level 0.45 :attack 0.002 :decay 0.08 :sustain 0 :release 0.05 }
    { :wave :pink :level 0.25 :attack 0.0005 :decay 0.006 :sustain 0 :release 0.006 } ]
  :modulation [ [ 1 0 1.5 ] ]
  :carriers [ 0 2 3 ]
  :velocity-sensitivity 0.5 :pan -0.1 :level 0.35 } :kick instrument-patch!

\ === the score ===
\ melodic parts are [ pitch length ... ], a pitch an array for a chord and :rest
\ for silence; lengths are fractions of a whole note, swung eighths written as
\ 1/6 then 1/12

\ the chords: an introduction of four bars, the melody's two eight-bar halves, two bars of ending
\ intro   Dm9 | Bbmaj7#11 | Gm9 | A7b9
\ first   Dm9 | Dm9 | Bbmaj7#11 | A7b9 | Gm9 | C13 | Fmaj9 | Em7b5 A7b9
\ second  Dm9 | Bbmaj7 | Gm9 | C7b9 | Fmaj9 | Bb7#11 | Em7b5 A7b9 | Dm(maj7)
\ ending  Dm(maj7) held

[ :rest 4
  :a4 3/8 :g4 1/8 :f4 1/4 :e4 1/4
  :d4 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :rest 1/4 :e4 1/6 :d4 1/12 :e4 1/4 :f4 1/4
  :bb4 1/2 :a4 1/4 :rest 1/4
  :a4 3/8 :bb4 1/8 :a4 1/4 :g4 1/4
  :f4 1/4 :e4 1/4 :rest 1/2
  :rest 1/4 :g4 1/6 :f4 1/12 :e4 1/4 :c4 1/4
  :d4 1/4 :c#4 1/2 :rest 1/4
  :rest 1/4 :f4 1/4 :a4 1/4 :c5 1/4
  :d5 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :bb4 3/8 :a4 1/8 :g4 1/4 :f4 1/4
  :e4 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :rest 1/4 :a4 3/4
  :ab4 3/8 :g4 1/8 :e4 1/4 :rest 1/4
  :a4 3/8 :g4 1/8 :f4 1/4 :e4 1/4
  :d4 3/2 :rest 3/2 ] to sax-part

[ [ :f3 :a3 :c4 :e4 ] 1
  [ :a3 :d4 :e4 ] 1
  [ :bb3 :d4 :f4 :a4 ] 1
  [ :g3 :bb3 :c#4 :f4 ] 1
  [ :f3 :a3 :c4 :e4 ] 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :rest 5/12 [ :f3 :b3 :e4 ] 7/12
  [ :a3 :d4 :e4 ] 3/4 :rest 1/4
  [ :g3 :bb3 :c#4 :f4 ] 1/2 :rest 1/2
  [ :bb3 :d4 :f4 :a4 ] 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :rest 5/12 [ :bb3 :d4 :e4 :a4 ] 7/12
  [ :a3 :c4 :e4 :g4 ] 3/4 :rest 1/4
  [ :g3 :bb3 :d4 ] 1/2 [ :g3 :bb3 :c#4 :f4 ] 1/2
  [ :f3 :a3 :c4 :e4 ] 1/2 :rest 1/2
  [ :a3 :d4 :f4 ] 3/4 :rest 1/4
  :rest 5/12 [ :bb3 :d4 :f4 :a4 ] 7/12
  [ :bb3 :db4 :e4 :a4 ] 1/2 :rest 1/2
  [ :a3 :c4 :e4 :g4 ] 1
  [ :ab3 :d4 :e4 :g4 ] 3/4 :rest 1/4
  [ :g3 :bb3 :d4 ] 1/2 [ :g3 :bb3 :c#4 :f4 ] 1/2
  [ :f3 :a3 :c#4 :e4 ] 1
  [ :d3 :f3 :a3 :c#4 :e4 ] 2 ] to piano-part

[ :a5 3/8 :g5 1/8 :f5 1/4 :e5 1/4
  :d5 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :bb4 3/8 :d5 1/8 :f5 1/4 :a5 1/4
  :g5 1/4 :f5 1/6 :e5 1/12 :c#5 1/2
  :rest 16
  :a5 1/6 :e5 1/12 :c#5 1/6 :a4 1/12 :f4 1/2
  :e5 1 ] to piano-fill-part

[ :d2 1/2 :a2 1/2  :bb1 1/2 :f2 1/2  :g2 1/2 :d2 1/2  :a1 1/2 :e2 1/4 :c#2 1/4
  :d2 1/2 :a2 1/2  :d2 1/2 :c2 1/2  :bb1 1/2 :f2 1/2  :a1 1/2 :e2 1/4 :a1 1/4
  :g1 1/2 :d2 1/2  :c2 1/2 :g2 1/4 :e2 1/4  :f2 1/2 :c2 1/4 :d#2 1/4  :e2 1/2 :a1 1/2
  :d2 1/2 :a2 1/2  :bb1 1/2 :f2 1/2  :g1 1/2 :d2 1/2  :c2 1/2 :e2 1/4 :g2 1/4
  :f2 1/2 :c2 1/2  :bb1 1/2 :d2 1/4 :f2 1/4  :e2 1/2 :a1 1/2  :d2 1/2 :a1 1/2
  :d2 2 ] to bass-part

\ drum parts are [ length strength ... ], strength 0 for silence, bar by bar

\ a bar's hits repeated over a number of bars
: bars-of ( bar n-bars -- hits )
	| bar n-bars |
	[ ] to hits
	0 n-bars 1 do k
		hits bar concat to hits
	loop
	hits ;

[ 1/2 0.7 1/2 0.55 ] 20 bars-of [ 1/2 0.5 1/2 0.4 1/2 0.3 1/2 0.2 ] concat to brush-part
\ the snare taps on two and four with a ghost on four's swung off-beat; a soft triplet on three at a phrase's end, on four at a section's end
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.55 1/4 0 1/6 0.6 1/12 0.25 ] to snare-plain
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.55 1/12 0.3 1/12 0.35 1/12 0.4 1/4 0.55 ] to snare-phrase-end
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.55 1/4 0 1/12 0.3 1/12 0.35 1/12 0.45 ] to snare-section-end
[ snare-plain snare-plain snare-plain snare-section-end
  snare-plain snare-plain snare-plain snare-phrase-end snare-plain snare-plain snare-plain snare-section-end
  snare-plain snare-plain snare-plain snare-phrase-end snare-plain snare-plain snare-plain snare-section-end
  [ 1/4 0.35 7/4 0 ]
] [ ] ' concat reduce to snare-part
\ the hi-hat on two and four, a swung pair or a triplet on four at a phrase's end, and a pickup into a triplet at a section's end
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.5 1/4 0 1/4 0.5 ] to hihat-plain
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.5 1/4 0 1/6 0.5 1/12 0.35 ] to hihat-pair
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.5 1/4 0 1/12 0.45 1/12 0.35 1/12 0.4 ] to hihat-triplet
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.5 1/6 0 1/12 0.35 1/12 0.5 1/12 0.35 1/12 0.45 ] to hihat-section-end
[ hihat-plain hihat-pair hihat-plain hihat-section-end
  hihat-plain hihat-pair hihat-plain hihat-triplet hihat-plain hihat-pair hihat-plain hihat-section-end
  hihat-plain hihat-pair hihat-plain hihat-triplet hihat-plain hihat-pair hihat-plain hihat-section-end
] [ ] ' concat reduce to hihat-part
[ 1/4 0.35 1/4 0 1/4 0.3 1/4 0 ] 20 bars-of [ 1/4 0.3 7/4 0 ] concat to kick-part

\ === queueing ===

\ a number in [-0.5, 0.5) fixed by k, so a performance is the same every time and draws nothing from the random stream
: variation ( k -- f ) 12.9898 * sin 43758.5453 * dup round-down - 0.5 - ;

\ queue a melodic part on an instrument, each note's velocity varied a little around the given one
: queue-part ( notes instrument velocity articulation -- )
	| notes instrument velocity articulation |
	instrument sequence-instrument
	articulation sequence-articulation
	0 notes size 2 do k
		notes k @i to pitch
		notes k 1 + @i to length
		pitch :rest = if length sequence-rest continue then
		k 0.37 * variation 0.1 * velocity + 0 1 clamp sequence-velocity
		pitch array? if pitch length sequence-chord else pitch length sequence-note then
	loop ;

\ queue a drum part on an instrument, each hit's strength varied a little
: queue-hits ( hits instrument articulation -- )
	| hits instrument articulation |
	instrument sequence-instrument
	articulation sequence-articulation
	0 hits size 2 do k
		hits k @i to length
		hits k 1 + @i to strength
		strength 0 = if length sequence-rest continue then
		k 0.53 * variation 0.08 * strength + 0 1 clamp sequence-velocity
		:c4 length sequence-note
	loop ;

\ every instrument back at its patch's level, sending all of itself to every effect, so a cue that changed one leaves no trace on the next
: standard-mix! ( -- )
	[ [ :sax 0.16 ] [ :clarinet 0.06 ] [ :piano 0.08 ] [ :piano-fill 0.08 ] [ :bass 0.36 ]
	  [ :brush 0.07 ] [ :snare 0.2 ] [ :hihat 0.9 ] [ :open-hihat 0.6 ] [ :kick 0.35 ] ]
	( entry |
		entry second :level entry first instrument!
		[ :chorus-send :delay-send :reverb-send ] ( send | 1 send entry first instrument! ) each
	) each ;

\ a melodic part moved by a number of semitones, chords and all
: shifted ( notes semitones -- notes )
	| notes semitones |
	( pitch>midi semitones + ) to shift-pitch
	[ 0 notes size 2 do k
		notes k @i to pitch
		pitch :rest = if :rest else pitch array? if pitch shift-pitch map else pitch pitch>midi semitones + then then
		notes k 1 + @i
	loop ] ;

\ the room: a small dark plate that takes little of the brush noise's brightness, a faint echo of each phrase at a dotted eighth, and a slow chorus
: theme-effects! ( -- )
	0.26 :wet :reverb effect! 1 :dry :reverb effect!
	0.5 :decay :reverb effect! 0.7 :size :reverb effect! 0.72 :damping :reverb effect!
	0.12 :wet :delay effect! 0.625 :time :delay effect! 0.28 :feedback :delay effect!
	0.12 :wet :chorus effect! 0.3 :rate :chorus effect! 0.002 :depth :chorus effect!
	0.02 :predelay :reverb effect! 0.4 :bandwidth :reverb effect!
	120 :low-cut :reverb effect! 4500 :high-cut :reverb effect!
	0.9 :level :master effect! ;

\ queue the whole theme from the present
: queue-theme ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	theme-effects!
	72 sequence-tempo
	sax-part :sax 0.72 0.97 queue-part
	piano-part :piano 0.5 0.92 queue-part
	piano-fill-part :piano-fill 0.6 0.9 queue-part
	bass-part :bass 0.75 0.85 queue-part
	brush-part :brush 1 queue-hits
	snare-part :snare 0.5 queue-hits
	hihat-part :hihat 0.5 queue-hits
	kick-part :kick 0.5 queue-hits ;

\ === exploring the house: a quiet loop ===
\ sixteen bars without the saxophone, soft enough to read over; its last bar
\ leads back to its first, so queueing it again as it ends plays on without a seam
\ bars 1-8   Dm9 | Dm9 | Ebmaj7#11 | Ebmaj7#11 | Dm9 | Dm9 | Bbmaj7 | A7b9
\ bars 9-16  Gm9 | Gm9 | Dm9 | Dm9 | Ebmaj7#11 | Ebmaj7#11 | Em7b5 A7b9 | A7b9

[ [ :f3 :a3 :c4 :e4 ] 3/2 :rest 1/2
  [ :g3 :a3 :d4 :f4 ] 1 :rest 5/12 [ :g3 :a3 :d4 :f4 ] 7/12
  [ :f3 :a3 :c4 :e4 ] 3/4 :rest 5/4
  [ :a3 :d4 :f4 ] 1/2 :rest 1/2 [ :g3 :bb3 :c#4 :f4 ] 1
  [ :bb3 :d4 :f4 :a4 ] 3/2 :rest 1/2
  [ :f3 :a3 :c4 :e4 ] 1 :rest 1
  [ :g3 :a3 :d4 :f4 ] 1 :rest 1
  [ :g3 :bb3 :d4 ] 1/2 [ :g3 :bb3 :c#4 :f4 ] 1 :rest 1/2 ] to house-piano-part

[ :rest 3/2 :e5 1/6 :d5 1/12 :a4 1/4
  :a4 1/2 :rest 3/2
  :rest 2
  :rest 1 :bb4 1/4 :a4 1/4 :c#5 1/2
  :rest 2
  :a5 3/8 :g5 1/8 :f5 1/4 :e5 1/4 :d5 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :rest 1 :d5 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :rest 2 ] to house-fill-part

[ :d2 1/2 :a2 1/2  :d2 1/2 :a1 1/2  :eb2 1/2 :bb1 1/2  :eb2 1/2 :bb1 1/2
  :d2 1/2 :a2 1/2  :d2 1/2 :c2 1/2  :bb1 1/2 :f2 1/2  :a1 1/2 :e2 1/4 :a1 1/4
  :g1 1/2 :d2 1/2  :g1 1/2 :d2 1/4 :c#2 1/4  :d2 1/2 :a2 1/2  :d2 1/2 :a1 1/2
  :eb2 1/2 :bb1 1/2  :eb2 1/2 :bb1 1/2  :e2 1/2 :a1 1/2  :a1 1/2 :e2 1/4 :c#2 1/4 ] to house-bass-part

\ the kit softer than in the theme: a triplet at the half's end and the loop's end
[ 1/2 0.5 1/2 0.4 ] 16 bars-of to house-brush-part
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.4 1/4 0 1/4 0.4 ] to house-snare-plain
[ house-snare-plain 7 bars-of
  [ 1/4 0 1/4 0.4 1/12 0.22 1/12 0.26 1/12 0.3 1/4 0.4 ]
  house-snare-plain 7 bars-of
  [ 1/4 0 1/4 0.4 1/4 0 1/12 0.22 1/12 0.26 1/12 0.32 ]
] [ ] ' concat reduce to house-snare-part
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.35 1/4 0 1/4 0.35 ] to house-hihat-plain
[ house-hihat-plain 7 bars-of
  [ 1/4 0 1/4 0.35 1/4 0 1/6 0.35 1/12 0.25 ]
  house-hihat-plain 7 bars-of
  [ 1/4 0 1/4 0.35 1/4 0 1/12 0.3 1/12 0.22 1/12 0.28 ]
] [ ] ' concat reduce to house-hihat-part
[ 1/4 0.22 3/4 0 ] 16 bars-of to house-kick-part

\ queue one pass of the house loop from the present, or from where the last pass ends
: queue-house-loop ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	theme-effects!
	72 sequence-tempo
	house-piano-part :piano 0.4 0.95 queue-part
	house-fill-part :piano-fill 0.45 0.9 queue-part
	house-bass-part :bass 0.6 0.85 queue-part
	house-brush-part :brush 1 queue-hits
	house-snare-part :snare 0.5 queue-hits
	house-hihat-part :hihat 0.5 queue-hits
	house-kick-part :kick 0.5 queue-hits ;

\ the house in the morning: a little quicker, the piano's answers an octave higher, the brushes lighter and no bass drum
: queue-house-morning ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	theme-effects!
	82 sequence-tempo
	0.05 :level :brush instrument!
	0.14 :level :snare instrument!
	house-piano-part :piano 0.4 0.95 queue-part
	house-fill-part 12 shifted :piano-fill 0.42 0.9 queue-part
	house-bass-part :bass 0.6 0.85 queue-part
	house-brush-part :brush 1 queue-hits
	house-snare-part :snare 0.5 queue-hits
	house-hihat-part :hihat 0.5 queue-hits ;

\ the house in the evening: slower, only the brushes, and the clarinet low and soft, a note every two bars stepping down the motif, A G F, then back to the A it began on, the fifth of Dm9; the second and third notes are held and then fall to a chord tone, G a step to the F of Bbmaj7 and F a third to the D of Gm9, each phrase a breath's length with a rest after it, and silence to the loop's end
[ :rest 4
  :a3 3/4 :rest 5/4
  :g3 1/2 :f3 1/4 :rest 5/4
  :f3 1/2 :d3 1/4 :rest 5/4
  :a3 3/4 :rest 5/4
  :rest 4 ] to house-evening-clarinet-part

: queue-house-evening ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	theme-effects!
	0.3 :wet :reverb effect! 0.6 :decay :reverb effect! 0.04 :predelay :reverb effect!
	66 sequence-tempo
	house-piano-part :piano 0.38 0.95 queue-part
	house-fill-part :piano-fill 0.4 0.9 queue-part
	house-bass-part :bass 0.55 0.85 queue-part
	house-evening-clarinet-part :clarinet 0.4 1 queue-part
	house-brush-part :brush 1 queue-hits
	house-snare-part :snare 0.5 queue-hits ;

\ === the grounds: an airy loop ===
\ sixteen bars at 60 beats a minute for piano and saxophone alone, in D Dorian;
\ the saxophone plays the motif at half speed, and the last bar leads back to the first
\ bars 1-8   Dm9 | G13 | Dm9 | G13 | Bbmaj7#11 | Am9 | Gm9 | A7sus4 A7b9
\ bars 9-16  Dm9 | G13 | Fmaj7#11 | Ebmaj7#11 | Dm9 | Bbmaj7 | Em7b5 | A7sus4

[ [ :d2 :a2 :e3 :f3 :c4 ] 1
  [ :g2 :f3 :b3 :e4 ] 1
  [ :d2 :a2 :e3 :f3 :c4 ] 1
  [ :g2 :f3 :b3 :e4 ] 1
  [ :bb1 :f2 :a3 :d4 :e4 ] 1
  [ :a2 :e3 :g3 :c4 ] 1
  [ :g2 :f3 :bb3 :d4 ] 1
