\ out of doors: a larger, wider plate than the house's whose tail starts late, as from far boundaries, and a clearer echo
: grounds-effects! ( -- )
	theme-effects!
	0.35 :wet :reverb effect! 0.76 :decay :reverb effect! 1.5 :size :reverb effect!
	0.06 :predelay :reverb effect! 1.5 :width :reverb effect!
	0.5 :bandwidth :reverb effect! 6000 :high-cut :reverb effect!
	0.18 :wet :delay effect! 0.75 :time :delay effect! 0.3 :feedback :delay effect! ;

\ queue one pass of the grounds loop from the present, or from where the last pass ends
: queue-grounds-loop ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	grounds-effects!
	60 sequence-tempo
	0.11 :level :sax instrument!
	grounds-piano-part :piano 0.38 1 queue-part
	grounds-fill-part :piano-fill 0.42 0.95 queue-part
	grounds-sax-part :sax 0.45 0.97 queue-part ;

\ === talking to people: a waltz ===
\ sixteen bars of 3/4 at 100 beats a minute in C minor, apart from the theme:
\ no saxophone, no motif, the piano in fourths, and no cadence, the harmony
\ swaying between Cm11 and the chord a half step above it
\ bars 1-8   Cm11 Cm11 | Dbmaj7#11 Dbmaj7#11 | Cm11 Cm11 | Dbmaj7#11 Dbmaj7#11
\ bars 9-16  Cm11 Cm11 | Abmaj7#11 Abmaj7#11 | Cm11 Cm11 | Dbmaj7#11 Dbmaj7#11

[ [ :f3 :bb3 :eb4 :g4 ] 3/4  :rest 1/4 [ :f3 :bb3 :eb4 :g4 ] 1/2
  [ :g3 :c4 :f4 :ab4 ] 3/2
  [ :f3 :bb3 :eb4 :g4 ] 3/4  :rest 1/4 [ :g3 :c4 :f4 :bb4 ] 1/2
  [ :g3 :c4 :f4 :ab4 ] 3/4  :rest 3/4
  [ :f3 :bb3 :eb4 :g4 ] 3/2
  [ :d3 :g3 :c4 :eb4 ] 3/4  :rest 1/4 [ :d3 :g3 :c4 :eb4 ] 1/2
  [ :f3 :bb3 :eb4 :g4 ] 3/4  :rest 3/4
  [ :g3 :c4 :f4 :ab4 ] 3/4  :rest 1/4 [ :g3 :c4 :f4 :ab4 ] 1/2 ] to waltz-piano-part

[ :rest 9/4 :rest 1/4 :f5 1/6 :eb5 1/12 :c5 1/4
  :rest 9/4 :rest 1/2 :g5 1/4
  :rest 9/4 :rest 1/4 :d5 1/4 :eb5 1/4
  :rest 9/4 :rest 1/4 :ab4 1/4 :g4 1/4 ] to waltz-fill-part

[ :c2 3/4  :g1 1/2 :bb1 1/6 :c2 1/12
  :db2 3/4  :ab1 3/4
  :c2 3/4  :g1 3/4
  :db2 3/4  :ab1 3/4
  :c2 3/4  :g1 1/2 :bb1 1/6 :a1 1/12
  :ab1 3/4  :eb2 1/2 :d2 1/6 :c#2 1/12
  :c2 3/4  :g1 3/4
  :db2 3/4  :ab1 1/2 :bb1 1/6 :b1 1/12 ] to waltz-bass-part

\ the hi-hat leads in three: the bass drum on one, the hat closed on two and its swung off-beat, half open and ringing on three, and in every other bar closed again on three's off-beat into the next one; a closed triplet on three at bars 8 and 16; under it a light brush sweep a bar and faint snare taps on two and three
[ 3/4 0.25 ] 16 bars-of to waltz-brush-part
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.22 1/4 0.18 ] 16 bars-of to waltz-snare-part
[ 1/4 0 1/6 0.45 1/12 0.3 1/6 0 1/12 0.3 ] to waltz-hihat-pickup
[ 1/4 0 1/6 0.45 1/12 0.3 1/4 0 ] to waltz-hihat-plain
[ 1/4 0 1/6 0.45 1/12 0.3 1/12 0.35 1/12 0.3 1/12 0.35 ] to waltz-hihat-triplet
[ waltz-hihat-pickup waltz-hihat-plain waltz-hihat-pickup waltz-hihat-plain waltz-hihat-pickup waltz-hihat-plain waltz-hihat-pickup waltz-hihat-triplet
  waltz-hihat-pickup waltz-hihat-plain waltz-hihat-pickup waltz-hihat-plain waltz-hihat-pickup waltz-hihat-plain waltz-hihat-pickup waltz-hihat-triplet
] [ ] ' concat reduce to waltz-hihat-part
[ 1/2 0 1/4 0.5 ] to waltz-open-plain
[ waltz-open-plain 7 bars-of [ 3/4 0 ] waltz-open-plain 7 bars-of [ 3/4 0 ]
] [ ] ' concat reduce to waltz-open-hihat-part
[ 1/4 0.22 1/2 0 ] 16 bars-of to waltz-kick-part

\ queue one pass of the waltz from the present, or from where the last pass ends
: queue-waltz-loop ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	theme-effects!
	100 sequence-tempo
	waltz-piano-part :piano 0.42 0.95 queue-part
	waltz-fill-part :piano-fill 0.45 0.9 queue-part
	waltz-bass-part :bass 0.6 0.85 queue-part
	waltz-brush-part :brush 1 queue-hits
	waltz-snare-part :snare 0.5 queue-hits
	waltz-hihat-part :hihat 0.5 queue-hits
	waltz-open-hihat-part :open-hihat 0.9 queue-hits
	waltz-kick-part :kick 0.5 queue-hits ;

\ === a discovery: a sting ===
\ about five seconds: a snare triplet into the downbeat, where the bass and the
\ bass drum land under a held D minor chord with its major seventh and the
\ saxophone climbs the motif's first four notes backwards, E F G A, holding the
\ A the theme begins on

[ :rest 1/4 :e4 1/4 :f4 1/12 :g4 1/12 :a4 1/2 ] to sting-sax-part
[ :rest 1/4 [ :d3 :a3 :c#4 :f4 ] 11/12 ] to sting-piano-part
[ :rest 1/4 :d2 1/2 ] to sting-bass-part
[ 1/12 0.2 1/12 0.28 1/12 0.36 ] to sting-snare-part
[ 1/4 0 11/12 0.35 ] to sting-brush-part
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.35 ] to sting-kick-part

\ queue the sting from the present
: queue-discovery-sting ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	theme-effects!
	72 sequence-tempo
	sting-sax-part :sax 0.62 1 queue-part
	sting-piano-part :piano 0.5 1 queue-part
	sting-bass-part :bass 0.7 0.85 queue-part
	sting-snare-part :snare 0.5 queue-hits
	sting-brush-part :brush 1 queue-hits
	sting-kick-part :kick 0.5 queue-hits ;

\ === something suspicious: a cue ===
\ two bars: the bass creeps down the motif at half speed, A G F E, stopping
\ unresolved on E under two chords built on tritones, with a soft high note on
\ three, a heartbeat on the bass drum and slow swells of the brush

[ :a2 1/2 :g2 1/2 :f2 1/2 :e2 1/2 ] to suspense-bass-part
[ [ :d3 :ab3 :c4 ] 1 [ :e3 :bb3 :d4 ] 1 ] to suspense-piano-part
[ :rest 1/2 :eb6 1/4 :rest 3/4 :a5 1/4 :rest 1/4 ] to suspense-fill-part
[ 1 0.4 1 0.5 ] to suspense-brush-part
[ 1/6 0.3 1/12 0.22 3/4 0 1/6 0.3 1/12 0.22 3/4 0 ] to suspense-kick-part

\ queue the cue from the present
: queue-suspense-cue ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	theme-effects!
	72 sequence-tempo
	suspense-bass-part :bass 0.65 0.9 queue-part
	suspense-piano-part :piano 0.45 1 queue-part
	suspense-fill-part :piano-fill 0.35 0.9 queue-part
	suspense-brush-part :brush 1 queue-hits
	suspense-kick-part :kick 0.5 queue-hits ;

\ === the hour turning: a time mark ===
\ six seconds at 120 beats a minute, so the clock is exact: the hi-hat ticks
\ every half second, stronger on each second, while the piano chimes the motif
\ high a second a note, A G F E, and lands on D over an open fifth and the bass's
\ low D left to ring, the one cue that completes the motif

[ :a5 1/2 :g5 1/2 :f5 1/2 :e5 1/2 :d5 1 ] to time-mark-fill-part
[ :rest 2 [ :d3 :a3 ] 1 ] to time-mark-piano-part
[ :rest 2 :d2 1 ] to time-mark-bass-part
[ 1/4 0.4 1/4 0.22 ] 4 bars-of to time-mark-hihat-part

\ queue the time mark from the present
: queue-time-mark ( -- )
	standard-mix!
	theme-effects!
	120 sequence-tempo
	time-mark-fill-part :piano-fill 0.5 0.95 queue-part
	time-mark-piano-part :piano 0.4 1 queue-part
	time-mark-bass-part :bass 0.7 1 queue-part
	time-mark-hihat-part :hihat 0.5 queue-hits ;

\ === a confrontation: a build that stops unresolved ===
\ eight bars at 94 beats a minute: the saxophone states the motif over a D
\ pedal, answers it a fourth higher over Gm9, and climbs to hold C#, the
\ leading note of A7b9, which the ending that follows resolves or leaves
\ bars 1-4  Dm(maj7) Dm(maj7) | Ebmaj7#11 Ebmaj7#11, over D
\ bars 5-8  Gm9 | Bb7#11 | Em7b5 | A7b9, held

[ :a4 3/8 :g4 1/8 :f4 1/4 :e4 1/4
  :d4 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :rest 2
  :d5 3/8 :c5 1/8 :bb4 1/4 :a4 1/4
  :g4 1/2 :rest 1/2
  :bb4 1/2 :a4 1/4 :g4 1/4
  :c#5 1 ] to confrontation-sax-part

\ a bar of stabs on the swung off-beats of two and four
: stabs ( chord -- notes )
	| chord |
	[ :rest 5/12 chord 1/12 :rest 5/12 chord 1/12 ] ;

[ [ :f3 :a3 :c#4 :e4 ] stabs [ :f3 :a3 :c#4 :e4 ] stabs
  [ :g3 :a3 :d4 ] stabs [ :g3 :a3 :d4 ] stabs
  [ :bb3 :d4 :f4 :a4 ] stabs [ :ab3 :d4 :e4 :g4 ] stabs
  [ :g3 :bb3 :d4 ] stabs [ [ :g3 :bb3 :c#4 :f4 ] 1 ]
] [ ] ' concat reduce to confrontation-piano-part

[ :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4   :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4 :c#2 1/4
  :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4   :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4 :d2 1/4
  :g1 1/4 :bb1 1/4 :d2 1/4 :bb1 1/4   :bb1 1/4 :d2 1/4 :f2 1/4 :e2 1/4
  :e2 1/4 :g2 1/4 :f2 1/4 :bb1 1/4   :a1 1 ] to confrontation-bass-part

\ the kit firmer than in the loops, the bass drum quickening from one and three to every beat, a triplet into the held last bar
[ 1/2 0.55 1/2 0.5 ] 7 bars-of [ 1 0.6 ] concat to confrontation-brush-part
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.6 1/4 0 1/6 0.6 1/12 0.3 ] 6 bars-of
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.6 1/4 0 1/12 0.35 1/12 0.45 1/12 0.55 ] concat [ 1 0 ] concat to confrontation-snare-part
[ 1/4 0 1/4 0.5 1/4 0 1/4 0.5 ] 7 bars-of [ 1 0 ] concat to confrontation-hihat-part
[ 1/4 0.3 1/4 0 1/4 0.28 1/4 0 ] 4 bars-of [ 1/4 0.3 1/4 0.25 1/4 0.3 1/4 0.25 ] 3 bars-of concat [ 1/4 0.35 3/4 0 ] concat to confrontation-kick-part

